# spec_id: eravos.organism.organ · version 1.0.0 · phase P8.3 · status canonical
# source: v10 _registerQOTSASynths gothic_organ/gothic_chord + QOTSA_PRESETS ("Hanging Tree")
identity:
  id: eravos.organ ; label: Gothic Organ ; icon: ⛪ ; accent: "#551188"
  comp_intent: Dark detuned pipe-organ drones and chords — slow-breathing, huge, haunted.
  novelty: Only additive organism — 9 drawbar partials per voice with per-rank detune and a 'breath' amplitude cycle; poly 6.
engine:
  voice: 9 sine/partials at footages 16',5⅓',8',4',2⅔',2',1⅗',1⅓',1' (ratios 0.5,1.5,1,2,3,4,5,6,8) ; drawbar levels 0..8 ; rank detune ± cents (celeste)
  pipe character: chiff (short BP noise on attack) ; wind noise (LP noise × breath) ; tremulant (amp LFO)
  breath: slow amp cycle (period 4–20 s or breath-organism sync) — the 'Hanging Tree' swell
  space: always feeds reverb send high by default (cathedral) ; sub-octave pedal on lowest held note
config: drawbars[9] 0..8 def [8,0,8,6,0,4,0,0,2] ; celeste 0..20 c def 7 ; chiff 0..1 ; wind 0..1 ; tremRate/depth ; breathPeriod 4..20 s ; breathDepth 0..1 ; attack/release ; pedal bool
presets: Hanging Tree (QOTSA_PRESETS), Cathedral Full, Flute 8', Eerie Celeste, Pedal Drone
hooks: STD.audio_out ; STD.note_in ; STD.midi_in ; STD.theory_in ; organ.hook.breath_in (in ; modulation ; port breath — from eravos.breath)
ui: hero = 9 draggable drawbars (brown/white/black like a console) ; breath meter ; keyboard
tests: drawbar only 8' → single partial at note f ± 0.5 Hz ; 7 notes held → 6 voices (oldest stolen) ; breath period 10 s measured on amp ± 2%

# ---- dependencies (generated by build/specs.mjs — do not edit by hand)
dependencies:
  mode: music   # Music Production
  toolbar_units: [music.engine, music.transport, music.tempo, music.key, music.meter, music.midi]   # ui expansion when added: Audio engine · Transport · Tempo · Song key · Master meter · MIDI button
  services:
    - audio: Audio engine — makes sound
    - clock: Master clock & tempo — locks to the beat
    - key: Song key & scale — plays in key
    - midi: MIDI input — plays from a controller (arm with the MIDI button)
    - mod: 1 modulation input — LFO / XY / Macro can move them
    - notes: Notes from a sequencer, timeline or keys — or play its own keyboard
  inputs:
    - organ.hook.note_in (note:trigger)
    - organ.hook.midi_in (midi:note) — ambient broadcast
    - organ.hook.theory_in (theory:key-change) — ambient broadcast
    - organ.hook.transport_in (transport:tick|transport:play|transport:stop) — ambient broadcast
    - organ.hook.breath_in (modulation · port mod.breath)
  outputs:
    - organ.hook.audio_out (audio · port out)
  permissions: [audio_out, midi_in, bus_publish, bus_subscribe]
  works_with: [eravos.breath, eravos.coven, eravos.fx-haunt, eravos.timeline, eravos.sequencer, eravos.midi-mapper, eravos.lyric-rhythm, eravos.ratio-lattice]

# 3.48 MOTION (phase P48.4 · status mapped · specs/eravos.motion.spec) — "the gothic organ … more dynamic"
findings: 27 settings, 1 mod input (breath); drawbars set one by one and jump; rotary fast/slow switches without inertia;
  no expression pedal.
adds:
  EXPRESSION (swell pedal): a 0–1 control on level + darkness (the box closing), audio-rate bus `expression`, mapped to
    MIDI CC11 / CC7 by default
  REGISTRATIONS: two drawbar sets A and B (9 bars each) and a 0–1 morph between them — drawbars glide, the morph is mod-able;
    the Swell + Registration macros make a sustained chord evolve by hand
  ROTARY with inertia: slow ↔ fast ramps the horn (≈0.8 s) and the drum (≈3 s) like a real cabinet; `rotorSpeed` becomes
    a continuous 0–1 (brake at 0)
  macros: Swell = expression · Registration = A↔B morph · Spin = rotor slow↔fast · Cathedral = space 0.2→1 + release 0.3→4 s
  perform pad: X = Swell, Y = Registration, spring-back off
  key velocity → chiff and percussion level (on/off as an option, organs are traditionally not velocity-sensitive)
  every setting can carry motion (M1)
acceptance: rotor slow→fast reaches full speed in 0.6–1.0 s (horn) and 2.5–3.5 s (drum), measured from the AM rate;
  registration morph 0→1 changes the spectrum continuously (no step > 1 dB in any partial over 10 ms)
